# Pinned sibling commits the worker makes present in the trusted clones before a run (aien-test worker,
# `ensure_pins`): `<repo> <source-repo> <sha40>`. A gate pins a sibling commit in its run script
# (`pin` in tests/gates/run.sh); the sandbox has no network, so a pinned commit that is not on a fetched
# branch must be fetched by its sha on the trusted side first. The worker fetches a missing one from the
# trusted clone's own origin and holds it as refs/remotes/aien-pins/<sha> (wt.sh sync copies that ref
# into the mirror). Read from the operator's trusted sc clone, beside `siblings`; never from the head.
# Pins that come from lock files (omega.lock and the locks inside it, cudapp.lock) are not listed: they follow main.
